From 2e68f618ae467bd058d0872f7dd770f13b130bf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:15:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] firmware: qcom: scm: QSEE app loading from firmware
 images (Galaxy Tab S3)

Mainline's qseecom interface only looks up and talks to apps the firmware
has already started (the UEFI secure app on recent laptops). Samsung's
MSM8996 tablets ship their QSEE apps as firmware images in the apnhlos
partition, loaded by the downstream qseecom driver: cmnlib (the services
library) through TZ_OS_LOAD_SERVICES_IMAGE_ID (app manager command 7),
then each app through TZ_OS_APP_START_ID (command 1), from a physically
contiguous buffer holding the .mdt followed by the segment files.

Add qcom_scm_qseecom_app_start() and
qcom_scm_qseecom_load_services_image() with those calls, and allowlist the
Galaxy Tab S3 (samsung,gts3lwifi, samsung,gts3llte).

qcom_qseecom_tabs3_test is a development module that loads cmnlib and one
app (default skeymast, Samsung's keymaster) from
qcom/msm8996/samsung/gts3/tz/ and logs the app ID. On an SM-T820 with
QSEE 0x1001000: cmnlib loads, skeymast starts as app 6 and is found by
the lookup afterwards.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
